# What research/tdd imports from research/lean-code, and the exact state it was read at.
#
# research/tdd/run.py does not vendor the generic arm, isolation, process and diff layer: it loads
# research/lean-code/run.py as a module (see that file's `lean()`). This PIN records what was read
# and when, so a reviewer can diff the dependency instead of guessing at it. The contract is not
# enforced by this file — it is enforced by `run.py --selftest`, group `contract`, which gates
# `--matrix`: no paid cell runs while an imported symbol is missing or has changed behaviour.
#
# KNOWN LIMIT: the contract test checks the symbols this harness relies on. A lean-code edit that
# keeps every signature and every checked behaviour but changes something else would not be caught.

